shape theory.algebra.emergent-existence : theory.landscape, theory.coherence.equivalence {
  type: theorem
  layer: 0
  """
// Theorem 16.15 (Emergent Existence).
// If shapes A_1...A_n persist, and coupling geometry S_D is
// coherent (satisfies Laws 0-3), then the emergent shape D with
// structure S_D exists and persists. No construction is required.
//
// This inverts the constructive approach. In ZF, an object exists
// only if constructed from below. In persistence structure, an
// object exists if its structure is coherent. Construction is one
// way to verify coherence but not the only way.
//
// Emergent Existence is the algebraic form of Landscape Completeness.
// The Laws of Coherence provide the verification conditions.
//
// Extends to infinite collections provided coupling geometry is
// coherent. Cardinality is not a limitation.
//
// Derives from: theory.landscape, theory.coherence.equivalence
  """
}
